[{"id":"VRCE-2-70-1","kanda":2,"kandaId":"ayodhya","sarga":70,"verse":1,"english":"As Bharata, the son of Kaikeyi was thus burning in grief, that foremost of those skilled in speech, the saint Vasistha, endowed with excellence of language, said.","alignment":{"type":"1:1","confidence":0.867,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-2-76-1"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"2070001","sanskritFile":"Ram02.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"8fc0a9bce5899806bc0091c8df4ee44906d45bb1411cb08669cced55431c8794","compact":"28f190aaa901bfebe6c635ee867c9744fbbf30a2bdd8e74db6996ba5be49cc46","nasal":"28f190aaa901bfebe6c635ee867c9744fbbf30a2bdd8e74db6996ba5be49cc46"}},{"id":"VRCE-2-70-2","kanda":2,"kandaId":"ayodhya","sarga":70,"verse":2,"english":"Do not weep, good betide you, O illustrious prince. Do you perform the funereal rites of the departed king.","alignment":{"type":"1:1","confidence":0.946,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-2-76-2"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"2070002","sanskritFile":"Ram02.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"a17a2eeb213fef1fc11a87e11f56921d03aa040475814112f569404cede0f09c","compact":"d7185711ead551feab159b1b6c6853cd1ab1341e500432331629ec82fe79313d","nasal":"d7185711ead551feab159b1b6c6853cd1ab1341e500432331629ec82fe79313d"}},{"id":"VRCE-2-70-3","kanda":2,"kandaId":"ayodhya","sarga":70,"verse":3,"english":"Hearing Vasistha's words, Bharata cognisant of duty, bowed down to the ground and despatched the ministers for performing the last rites.","alignment":{"type":"1:1","confidence":0.613,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-2-76-3"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"2070003","sanskritFile":"Ram02.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"0561361c0a91fa9911eb946865e032a6ac30e4bfe8de91c28d4ba4404023b660","compact":"cbd27f09e7a0fd048203dd6aa88c9be9693d5459660bc827dc82e81f2589a71f","nasal":"cbd27f09e7a0fd048203dd6aa88c9be9693d5459660bc827dc82e81f2589a71f"}},{"id":"VRCE-2-70-4","kanda":2,"kandaId":"ayodhya","sarga":70,"verse":4,"english":"And raising from under the oil the body of the king with a sallow countenance, and appearing to be asleep. Bharata placed it on the ground upon a couch in front adorned with various gems. Then overwhelmed with grief, Dasaratha's son bewailed him thus.","alignment":{"type":"grouped","confidence":0.712,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-2-76-4"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"2070004","sanskritFile":"Ram02.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"bdce5d78e09d9d67ff965214800fe4c47692bc826247c79788feedef6ac9d2d3","compact":"368e4d6cb90bec521eebc85c4d0f05c848ed53760bbf0e7e11814f957d3f9c14","nasal":"368e4d6cb90bec521eebc85c4d0f05c848ed53760bbf0e7e11814f957d3f9c14"}},{"id":"VRCE-2-70-5","kanda":2,"kandaId":"ayodhya","sarga":70,"verse":5,"english":"And raising from under the oil the body of the king with a sallow countenance, and appearing to be asleep. Bharata placed it on the ground upon a couch in front adorned with various gems. Then overwhelmed with grief, Dasaratha's son bewailed him thus.","alignment":{"type":"grouped","confidence":0.966,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-2-76-4"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"2070005","sanskritFile":"Ram02.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"eb35fb043f788c1f5fed8a57147292e2f92564ff41b4ba4de3c4ce58dcb3bf82","compact":"9a286aa725e10b102c3eec9fbac0fcf227e281a58bdb21498959a2464043dfd5","nasal":"9a286aa725e10b102c3eec9fbac0fcf227e281a58bdb21498959a2464043dfd5"}},{"id":"VRCE-2-70-6","kanda":2,"kandaId":"ayodhya","sarga":70,"verse":6,"english":"O king, what was it that you had intended to do, I absent and away from home, by banishing righteous Rāma and the powerful Lakşmana?","alignment":{"type":"1:1","confidence":1.0,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-2-76-5"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"2070006","sanskritFile":"Ram02.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"5e5f2e25b2009c47ae55dd7707e4ef11c1a729980bc617e6614214fad51d864e","compact":"1b68ab04d8dfd92596517563d1c898073e4fc4cad9480dcf782fa2386a8f5dbf","nasal":"1b68ab04d8dfd92596517563d1c898073e4fc4cad9480dcf782fa2386a8f5dbf"}},{"id":"VRCE-2-70-7","kanda":2,"kandaId":"ayodhya","sarga":70,"verse":7,"english":"Whither wend you, O mighty monarch, forsaking these aggrieved people, who have already been deprived of the lion like Rāma energetic in action?","alignment":{"type":"1:1","confidence":0.742,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-2-76-6"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"2070007","sanskritFile":"Ram02.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"72a842aee43cbd164c7c82a1e29c90dbf030eb169444a29c6d6f86ddae028e3c","compact":"862b2c4ad105c39007dfa3a96db0c45d4fdc8a7610659dd7c5a786eeac687b1f","nasal":"862b2c4ad105c39007dfa3a96db0c45d4fdc8a7610659dd7c5a786eeac687b1f"}},{"id":"VRCE-2-70-8","kanda":2,"kandaId":"ayodhya","sarga":70,"verse":8,"english":"O father, you having ascended heaven and Rāma having taken refuge in the woods, who now in this city of yours shall protect what the people possess and secure to them what they have not?","alignment":{"type":"1:1","confidence":0.818,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-2-76-7"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"2070008","sanskritFile":"Ram02.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"53fcb6eeb67030bb59a81dd55c3db91a326cfd24d7e7367d5fadb4e01fb18d13","compact":"ef98793e44905f6961ae6bfc4fb69983f6c225b49daf793f6e8773e17eb17966","nasal":"ef98793e44905f6961ae6bfc4fb69983f6c225b49daf793f6e8773e17eb17966"}},{"id":"VRCE-2-70-9","kanda":2,"kandaId":"ayodhya","sarga":70,"verse":9,"english":"Widowed in consequence of losing you, this earth does not look graceful. The city appears to me like the night deprived of the Moon","alignment":{"type":"1:1","confidence":0.86,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-2-76-8"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"2070009","sanskritFile":"Ram02.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"c83f80a540f9b974dd4b40cfcee4e09166c87a5bf8e8de8b677abd41d213aa9e","compact":"f4319ea235f9adbaa1edc27971bf9bbd07e7ecfb942a8a3937618ebb773384c4","nasal":"ff6349c6ef0a99381f94a2a35325d0da8b19a28a2370a24966af668aab9f5447"}},{"id":"VRCE-2-70-10","kanda":2,"kandaId":"ayodhya","sarga":70,"verse":10,"english":"As Bharata was lamenting thus in dejected mood, the mighty ascetic Vasiştha again addressed him, saying.","alignment":{"type":"1:1","confidence":0.906,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-2-76-9"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"2070010","sanskritFile":"Ram02.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"d8166d7fda0a23504a0950f3078e3d0469fcd12ef8646865cdc9c4f22c11696c","compact":"c8d23377e37c6568f5407c1b6725bf68d9d9f6f3802ecf633b2500ac905825b0","nasal":"c8d23377e37c6568f5407c1b6725bf68d9d9f6f3802ecf633b2500ac905825b0"}},{"id":"VRCE-2-70-11","kanda":2,"kandaId":"ayodhya","sarga":70,"verse":11,"english":"O mighty armed one, do you without indulging in any reflections, perform those funeral ceremonies of the monarch which ought to be performed.","alignment":{"type":"1:1","confidence":1.0,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-2-76-10"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"2070011","sanskritFile":"Ram02.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"7f27f2450493cbda554214a91614e8072fa93b92fed2fd9e40f6485059aed196","compact":"12ae3641fffa8d4637d3567d21075a9047bd6eaca2f759a11304358fde80a506","nasal":"cbec7cddcbfcb309bbfc541573f644788b806133de2cf0afcfc364cfd1ab5e16"}},{"id":"VRCE-2-70-12","kanda":2,"kandaId":"ayodhya","sarga":70,"verse":12,"english":"Thereupon honouring his words by saying, \"So be it,” he urged speed upon all the Rtvigs, priests, and Acāryas.","alignment":{"type":"1:1","confidence":0.761,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-2-76-11"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"2070012","sanskritFile":"Ram02.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"9a76e6fd9f0872eefb8b3528ac2472e6829b8f780c83a6abf2b687f9c25dfa92","compact":"f977a9070ffc26ef40315d8ec3d1f280fca7ca5701fe375205cf725540bf7a14","nasal":"f977a9070ffc26ef40315d8ec3d1f280fca7ca5701fe375205cf725540bf7a14"}},{"id":"VRCE-2-70-13","kanda":2,"kandaId":"ayodhya","sarga":70,"verse":13,"english":"And then those that had brought the king's corpse out side from the fire chamber, instructed by the Rtvigs and priests according to the ordinance began to offer oblations into the fire.","alignment":{"type":"1:1","confidence":0.64,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-2-76-12"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"2070013","sanskritFile":"Ram02.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"adb68b465b8d4d08121a58e856289b9f9ba5d19d528b2c2f97f302b0fc1dd896","compact":"dedafb2bca73168e5abfcc502291fa8d1a1c984a5e668f1cc0d3a28ad1c9fee3","nasal":"8d13283bc41e8c25a758d883c314f82f9c4c96bf1efe07c5cd9091fe8415b43a"}},{"id":"VRCE-2-70-14","kanda":2,"kandaId":"ayodhya","sarga":70,"verse":14,"english":"Next placing the king deprived of life on a car, the servants with their throats oppressed with vapour and with their minds weighed down with dejection carried him.","alignment":{"type":"1:1","confidence":0.764,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-2-76-13"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"2070014","sanskritFile":"Ram02.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"73a49b7c25506f979f